2|0@ToolBand^1440686469#cuhhcj4:pataksjalfrezi$:vicarious is an interesting song. i dont think its about vicious schadenfreude as it appears to be on the surface, although that is tangentially related to its real substance. i think its about how we eat meat, and we use cell phones made with child labor. that kind of thing. we need to get in touch with that. sometimes in order for you to survive and keep your loved ones safe, someone else has to get the short end of the stick. people like to ignore this, even to delude themselves into not being aware of it. what if there is an intruder in your house? what if someone is threatening the life of a loved one? what if you have to choose between that one aggressor dying and two of your loved ones dying? in this world, unfortunately, sometimes, these choices need to be made. these choices may not be inevitable in the potentials of the future. it doesn't have to be a zero sum thing. it is conceivable that we could create a society where delicious protein subtitutes are manufactured, prosperity is everywhere, and violence is largely abandoned. getting there is the greatest puzzle in history but it's not impossible. in the mean time, people should be in touch with these choices. i think that's what vicarious is about.
